course: dictionary
lesson: 2855
title: Doggy: a friendly word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can change its meaning a little, depending on the words around it. «Doggy» is a friendly, informal word, and small children often use it for a dog. The words after it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Look at the doggy!» means look at the dog, so doggy is a thing here. «A doggy smell» describes something as smelling like a dog, so doggy describes the smell. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases are fixed, so the whole phrase has a special meaning. A «doggy bag» is not a bag for dogs; it is a box for taking home food you did not finish. «Gone to doggy heaven» is a gentle, half-joking way to tell a child that a dog has died. The words around it, gone and heaven, give you the clue.
fact: «Doggy» is informal, so it is a friendly everyday word, often a child's word for dog. It can also be spelled «doggie».
fact: As a noun, «doggy» means a dog: «Look at the doggy!»
fact: As an adjective, «doggy» means like a dog or to do with dogs: «a doggy smell».
fact: A «doggy bag» is a bag or box to take home the food you did not finish at a restaurant.
fact: «Doggy paddle» is a simple way of swimming, paddling with your hands under the water like a dog.
exercise: «Look at the doggy!» What does doggy mean here? | *A dog | A way of swimming | A bag for leftover food | A dog door
exercise: After a restaurant meal, Sam asks for a «doggy bag». What is it? | A coat for a dog | *A box to take home food you did not finish | A bag for walking the dog | A bowl for water
exercise: Mia paddles her hands under the water to swim, just like a dog. What is this swimming style called? | *Doggy paddle | A doggy bag | Doggy heaven | A doggy door
test: «He has a doggy smell after the rain.» What kind of word is doggy here? | *An adjective, describing a smell | An adverb, meaning very quickly | A noun, meaning a dog | A verb, meaning to run
test: «Gone to doggy heaven» is a gentle way to tell a child what? | The dog is lost | *A dog has died | Someone has won a prize | The dog is very clean
exam: Which sentence uses doggy to mean a dog? | Put the leftovers in a doggy bag | *The little doggy wagged its tail in the park | Learn to swim with the doggy paddle | Her coat has a doggy smell
